<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Pomesanians</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1236 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Prussian people on the east bank of the lower Vistula, the first to be conquered by the Teutonic Knights in the 1230s.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Pomesanians lived in Pomesania, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nogat">Nogat</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drweca">Drwęca</a>, in what is now northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. Like other Prussian groups they emerged as a distinct territory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a>, with farming villages and hillforts and contacts with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-pomerania">Pomerania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masovia">Masovia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were organised in districts led by nobles rather than a single ruler, and kept the Prussian pagan cults. Their nearness to Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-pomerania">Pomerania</a> exposed them to missions and raids from the early 13th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, invited by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konrad-i-of-masovia">Konrad of Masovia</a>, attacked Pomesania first, founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwidzyn">Kwidzyn</a> (Marienwerder) in 1233 and winning at the Sirgune river in 1234; by 1236 the land was subdued. The Pomesanians joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-prussian-uprising">Great Prussian Uprising</a> in 1260 but were reconquered, and their land became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bishopric-of-pomesania">Bishopric of Pomesania</a> and Order territory.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/pomesanians.jpg" alt="Pomesanians" width="320" height="306"><figcaption>Image: JakaśKreatywnaNazwa123 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pomezania_na_mapie_adm._Polski.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1236 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Baltic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Prussian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pomesania, Pamedė</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1018&amp;focus=pomesanians" aria-label="Pomesanians on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5130 374 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Pomesanians lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5451 561h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5450 630h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5450 630h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Poland. <a href="/atlas?year=1018&amp;focus=pomesanians">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

